blocks.english:
Love, fear, a sincere mind,
Zeal, faith and true hope
Sound together in equal melody;

Here the hesitant learns to follow Christ;
From him the sinner shall learn
To shed righteous tears.

There, to help his neighbour,
To love God alone;
And us whom the world holds fast

As he fished, grace drew him
To the work of a fisher
Of a more worthy catch;

For He who commands fishing thus
Wills that the fish whom the nets take
Be preserved for life;

He prefers truth to vanities,
Leaves the net, leaves the boat,
Indeed leaves everything;

And, O happy Bar-Jona,
For these things Christ promises thee
Good things, the kingdoms above;

And while thou dost tread the waves of the sea,
He holds thee, wavering, with a faithful hand,
That thou mayest not sink;

When Christ’s question is raised,
He encloses in a brief utterance
The necessary faith;

Nay, by a wondrous lot,
Peter, thou shalt bind what is to be bound,
And what thou shalt loose shall be ratified;

Christ entrusts thee with the keys
To which the gate of heaven yields,
Whether thou open or close it;

And what is bound here
The supreme Judge willed
To be bound above the stars;

Thou dost enjoy the converse
Of the transfigured Messiah,
And of Moses and Elias together;
Thinking it sweet to remain here,
If only it were always granted
To be in this company;

Peter afterwards, a faithful companion
Of the Saviour, desires to die
Together with the Lord;

Zeal is the spur of love;
But a fall is also
A continual reminder of fear,

Which Christ foretold would happen to thee,
Lest confidence should overwhelm thee
In thy security;

What he sinned in denying thrice,
Love again expiated,
And a threefold confession;

But before Christ gives him
His dear flock to feed,
He weighs the law of charity;

Lacking gold and silver,
Afterwards in a moment he gives
Strong limbs to the lame man;

He gives Aeneas health,
And here and there bears deliverance
To the sick and miserable;

He exercises strict care of the flock,
And strikes the defrauding spouses
With a heavy punishment;

But idle Herod, who gives guards
To the captive, is deceived
Together with his attendant;

For, released from his bonds,
Peter now goes free,
Surrounded by a faithful companion;

As the magician hates Peter,
So Peter exposes Simon
For his shameful crime;

For while he seeks to fly,
He perishes openly by a grievous fall,
With the people looking on;

And while the cross is prepared for Peter,
He rejoices indeed to be crucified
With the Lord;

Open the doors to thy flock,
Which knows that this great right
Of the keys belongs to thee;
